{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebClosure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebClosure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebClosure.e_mul_prod_eq_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebClosure.e_mul_prod_eq_smul","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebClosure.lean#L86-L102","doc":"**The δ rule, abstractly.** On a word `pre ++ k :: post` whose prefix is all\nfar from `k`, left multiplication by `e_k` returns the same word scaled by `δ`.\n\nThis is the mechanism behind the measured `loops = 1 ⟺ k ∈ I ∧ k-1 ∉ I`:\n`k ∈ I` puts `k` at a block top, and `k-1 ∉ I` forces every earlier block's\nletters to be `≤ k-2` — exactly `hpre`. The `post` part is untouched, which is\nwhy the resulting normal form is *unchanged* rather than merely equivalent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebClosure.e_comm_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebClosure.e_comm_prod","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebClosure.lean#L65-L84","doc":"**`e_k` commutes past a whole word all of whose letters are far from `k`.**\n\nThe engine the δ rule rests on. Stated for an arbitrary list rather than for a\nnormal form, so the instantiation is a separate obligation and this stays\nreusable. ","signatureChunk":0}]}